{
  // SECURITY: `role` and `business_id` carry FIELD-LEVEL write RLS locking them
  // to role `admin` — the tier the service role evaluates as. Without this lock
  // any authenticated user could call auth.updateMe({ role: "admin" }) and
  // become a platform-wide admin (every tenant entity carries an unscoped
  // user_condition:{role:"admin"} RLS branch, which is what lets the backend
  // Safe functions write at all), or updateMe({ business_id: "<any id>" }) to
  // walk into another restaurant's data without its invite code.
  //
  // NOTE — no entity-level "rls" block here, deliberately. The built-in User is
  // managed by Base44's auth system and does not support one: adding it makes
  // asServiceRole.entities.User.update() hang rather than throw, so onboarding
  // dies with an empty-bodied HTTP 500 and no usable error. Field-level rls on
  // role/business_id is the supported — and the security-relevant — half.
  // scripts/validate-rls.mjs fails the build if either half drifts.
  //
  // All legitimate changes flow through service-role backend functions:
  //   complete-onboarding — create a restaurant, or FILE a join request with an
  //                         invite code (pending_business_id; grants nothing)
  //   manage-member       — approve/reject a join request (the only place a
  //                         code-joiner gets business_id, with a role picked by
  //                         the owner), promote/demote/remove a member
  //
  // DEPLOY ORDER: deploy those functions FIRST, then this schema. If the lock
  // lands before they are live, onboarding silently no-ops — Base44 drops
  // disallowed field writes without raising an error, so a new user just gets
  // stuck on the setup screen with no visible failure.
  //
  // The role model (Module 2, layer 2) is declared in src/lib/rbac.js — this
  // enum is the backend half of the same mapping and must stay in sync with it.
  "name": "User",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "role": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "admin",
        "business_admin",
        "staff"
      ],
      "default": "staff",
      "description": "Rol del usuario. 'admin' es el nivel de plataforma ACACIA (no un rol de inquilino); 'business_admin' es el dueño/gerente del restaurante; 'staff' es el personal de cocina que captura gastos, inventario y cortes.",
      "rls": {
        "write": {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "business_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Negocio (Business.id) al que pertenece el usuario. Un usuario pertenece a un solo negocio: lo asigna complete-onboarding y sólo manage-member (remove) lo limpia.",
      "rls": {
        "write": {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "pending_business_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Solicitud de unión pendiente: Business.id al que la persona pidió entrar con un código de invitación. NO da acceso a nada: ninguna regla RLS ni _guard.ts lo lee, sólo business_id cuenta. Lo escribe complete-onboarding (join) y lo limpia manage-member (aprobar/rechazar/quitar) o la propia persona (cancelar). Bloqueado a admin (sólo escriben las funciones de servicio) para que nadie pueda inventar solicitudes a nombre de otra persona ni saltarse la aprobación del dueño.",
      "rls": {
        "write": {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "join_requested_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Cuándo se envió la solicitud de unión (se muestra al dueño al aprobar). Va junto a pending_business_id y con el mismo bloqueo.",
      "rls": {
        "write": {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "last_active_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Última actividad significativa (actualizada con throttle ≥ 15 min)"
    }
  },
  "required": []
}
